IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `eia-core-interpretation`

-- Employment Insurance Act (S.C. 1996, c. 23), Part VIII.4 (Employment Insurance Emergency Response Benefit):
-- the Social Insurance Number (s 153.12), the end of an earlier benefit period (ss 153.121, 153.13), the adaptations
-- of ss 44, 50, 52, 112, 112.1, 126 and 138 and of reg 27 (ss 153.1301 to 153.13091), the write-off of amounts wrongly
-- paid (s 153.1306), the special rules (s 153.1310) and the cessation of effect (s 153.14).
-- Written by piece ei6 (Sonnet 5.5) on 2026-10-24.
-- Text: the unofficial plain-text rendering of the Justice Laws consolidation current to 2026-09-30; nothing here is
-- claimed to be verified against the official text.
--
-- Seat: the person who received, or is asked to repay, the emergency response benefit, or who wants to challenge a
-- decision about it.
--
-- NAMES. The adaptations change provisions of the Act outside this piece (ss 44, 50, 52, 112, 112.1, 126, 138). They
-- are named here "s 153.13NN as adapted s N(M) ...", so that none of them can clash with the rule that piece
-- ei1, ei3 or ei4 writes for the unadapted section.
--
-- CESSATION. Every adaptation takes a BOOLEAN, "the adaptation has not ceased to apply under section 153.14", which the
-- caller gets from `s 153.14 the provision still applies on the day` below: it asks on which day the adapted rule is
-- being applied, and the answer is FALSE for the adapted rule once the cessation day has passed (fork F-ei6-9). Where it
-- is FALSE the adapted provision says nothing; the unadapted section of the Act (outside this piece) may still decide.

§ `Section 153.14 - cessation of effect`

-- The provisions added by the nine Interim Orders listed in s 153.14, and the adaptations they make, cease to apply on
-- the earlier of June 2, 2027 and the day the Interim Order that enacted the provision is repealed. Which Interim Order
-- enacted a provision is not in the text, and nor is a repeal date: both are inputs. "Ceases to apply on D" is read as:
-- the provision applies through D and not after (assumed, not ruled: fork F-ei6-7 in NOTES.md).
-- src:2956 | 153.14 A provision of this Part that is added by any of the following Interim Orders or a provision that, under any of those Interim Orders, is an adaptation of a provision of this Act or provides for the non-application of a provision of this Act ceases to apply on the earlier of June 2, 2027 and the day on which the Interim Order that enacted the provision is repealed:
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.14 (src:2956)
GIVETH A DATE
`s 153.14 the latest day on which a provision added by an Interim Order may cease to apply` MEANS YearMonthDay 2027 6 2

-- src:2956 | 153.14 A provision of this Part that is added by any of the following Interim Orders or a provision that, under any of those Interim Orders, is an adaptation of a provision of this Act or provides for the non-application of a provision of this Act ceases to apply on the earlier of June 2, 2027 and the day on which the Interim Order that enacted the provision is repealed:
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.14 (src:2956)
GIVEN `the day on which the Interim Order that enacted the provision was repealed, if it has been` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `s 153.14 the day on which the provision ceases to apply` IS
    CONSIDER `the day on which the Interim Order that enacted the provision was repealed, if it has been`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `s 153.14 the latest day on which a provision added by an Interim Order may cease to apply`
    WHEN JUST repeal THEN
        IF repeal LESS THAN `s 153.14 the latest day on which a provision added by an Interim Order may cease to apply`
        THEN repeal
        ELSE `s 153.14 the latest day on which a provision added by an Interim Order may cease to apply`

-- src:2956 | 153.14 A provision of this Part that is added by any of the following Interim Orders or a provision that, under any of those Interim Orders, is an adaptation of a provision of this Act or provides for the non-application of a provision of this Act ceases to apply on the earlier of June 2, 2027 and the day on which the Interim Order that enacted the provision is repealed:
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.14 (src:2956)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      `the day on which the Interim Order that enacted the provision was repealed, if it has been` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 153.14 the provision still applies on the day` IF
    day AT MOST `s 153.14 the day on which the provision ceases to apply` `the day on which the Interim Order that enacted the provision was repealed, if it has been`

§ `Section 153.12 - the Social Insurance Number`

-- src:2879 | 153.12 The Minister is authorized to collect and use, for the purposes of the administration and enforcement of this Part, the Social Insurance Number of a claimant who makes a claim under this Part.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.12 (src:2879)
GIVEN `the person makes a claim under Part VIII.4` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose is the administration and enforcement of Part VIII.4` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 153.12 the Minister may collect and use the Social Insurance Number of the claimant` IF
        `the person makes a claim under Part VIII.4`
    AND `the purpose is the administration and enforcement of Part VIII.4`

§ `Sections 153.121 and 153.13 - the benefit period`

-- (1): a benefit period established before March 15, 2020 (including one under Part VIII) ends the day before the first
-- week for which the emergency response benefit is paid. (2): not if, after a reconsideration under s 112, a decision
-- that results in a benefit period beginning before March 15, 2020 is rendered after the benefit has been paid.
-- src:2883 | 153.121 (1) A benefit period that was established for a claimant before March 15, 2020 — including a benefit period established in respect of benefits payable under Part VIII — ends the day before the first week for which the claimant is paid an employment insurance emergency response benefit.
-- src:2884 | Reconsideration
-- src:2885 | (2) Despite subsection (1), if, following a reconsideration carried out under section 112, a decision that results in a benefit period being established that begins before March 15, 2020 is rendered after the claimant has been paid an employment insurance emergency response benefit, the benefit period does not end and the claimant is deemed to have not been eligible for the employment insurance emergency response benefit by reason of paragraph 153.9(2)(a).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.121(1), (2) (src:2883-2885)
GIVEN `the first day of the benefit period established for the claimant` IS A DATE
      `the Sunday that begins the first week for which the claimant is paid the emergency response benefit` IS A DATE
      `a decision that results in a benefit period beginning before March 15, 2020 is rendered after a reconsideration under section 112 and after the claimant has been paid the benefit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `s 153.121(1) the last day of the benefit period` IS
    IF     `the first day of the benefit period established for the claimant` LESS THAN (YearMonthDay 2020 3 15)
       AND NOT (`a decision that results in a benefit period beginning before March 15, 2020 is rendered after a reconsideration under section 112 and after the claimant has been paid the benefit`)
    THEN JUST (`the Sunday that begins the first week for which the claimant is paid the emergency response benefit` MINUS 1)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2885 | (2) Despite subsection (1), if, following a reconsideration carried out under section 112, a decision that results in a benefit period being established that begins before March 15, 2020 is rendered after the claimant has been paid an employment insurance emergency response benefit, the benefit period does not end and the claimant is deemed to have not been eligible for the employment insurance emergency response benefit by reason of paragraph 153.9(2)(a).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.121(2) (src:2885)
GIVEN `a decision that results in a benefit period beginning before March 15, 2020 is rendered after a reconsideration under section 112 and after the claimant has been paid the benefit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 153.121(2) the benefit period does not end and the claimant is deemed not to have been eligible by reason of paragraph 153.9(2)(a)` IF
    `a decision that results in a benefit period beginning before March 15, 2020 is rendered after a reconsideration under section 112 and after the claimant has been paid the benefit`

-- 153.13: the weeks during which the benefit was paid are not taken into account in establishing the benefit period.
-- A week is identified by the DATE of its Sunday.
-- src:2887 | 153.13 When a benefit period is being established for a claimant who has received an employment insurance emergency response benefit, in establishing the benefit period, the weeks during which the benefit was paid is not to be taken into account.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.13 (src:2887)
GIVEN `the weeks otherwise taken into account in establishing the benefit period` IS A LIST OF DATE
      `the weeks during which the emergency response benefit was paid` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A LIST OF DATE
DECIDE `s 153.13 the weeks taken into account in establishing the benefit period` IS
    filter (GIVEN w YIELD NOT (elem w `the weeks during which the emergency response benefit was paid`)) `the weeks otherwise taken into account in establishing the benefit period`

§ `Section 153.1301 - section 44 as adapted: returning an overpayment`

-- src:2891 | 153.1301 For the purposes of applying paragraph 153.6(1)(a), section 44 of the English version is adapted as follows:
-- src:2892 | Liability to return overpayment44A person who has received or obtained an employment insurance emergency response benefit payment for which the person is not eligible, or an employment insurance emergency response benefit payment in excess of the amount for which the person is eligible, shall without delay return the amount, the excess amount or the special warrant for payment of the amount, as the case may be.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.1301 (src:2891-2892)
GIVEN `the adaptation has not ceased to apply under section 153.14` IS A BOOLEAN
      `has received or obtained an emergency response benefit payment for which the person is not eligible` IS A BOOLEAN
      `has received an emergency response benefit payment in excess of the amount for which the person is eligible` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 153.1301 as adapted s 44 the person must return the amount without delay` IF
        `the adaptation has not ceased to apply under section 153.14`
    AND (   `has received or obtained an emergency response benefit payment for which the person is not eligible`
         OR `has received an emergency response benefit payment in excess of the amount for which the person is eligible`)

-- The amount to return: the whole payment if the person is not eligible, the excess if they are eligible for less.
-- The adapted text also names "the special warrant for payment of the amount", which is a thing to return, not a sum.
-- src:2891 | 153.1301 For the purposes of applying paragraph 153.6(1)(a), section 44 of the English version is adapted as follows:
-- src:2892 | Liability to return overpayment44A person who has received or obtained an employment insurance emergency response benefit payment for which the person is not eligible, or an employment insurance emergency response benefit payment in excess of the amount for which the person is eligible, shall without delay return the amount, the excess amount or the special warrant for payment of the amount, as the case may be.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.1301 (src:2891-2892)
GIVEN `the adaptation has not ceased to apply under section 153.14` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is eligible for the emergency response benefit payment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount of the payment received or obtained` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount for which the person is eligible` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `s 153.1301 as adapted s 44 the amount to be returned` IS
    BRANCH IF NOT (`the adaptation has not ceased to apply under section 153.14`) THEN NOTHING
           IF NOT (`the person is eligible for the emergency response benefit payment`) THEN JUST `the amount of the payment received or obtained`
           IF `the amount of the payment received or obtained` GREATER THAN `the amount for which the person is eligible` THEN JUST (`the amount of the payment received or obtained` MINUS `the amount for which the person is eligible`)
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

§ `Section 153.1302 - section 50 as adapted: information and attendance`

-- src:2894 | 153.1302 For the purposes of applying paragraph 153.6(1)(a), section 50 is adapted as follows:
-- src:2895 | Eligibility — employment insurance emergency response benefit50(1)A claimant who does not provide the Minister with the required information in respect of a claim for the employment insurance emergency response benefit or fails to comply with the requirement under subsection (2) is not eligible for the employment insurance emergency response benefit until they provide the information or comply with the requirement.Making claim or providing information in person(2)The Commission may require a claimant or group or class of claimants to be at a suitable place at a suitable time in order to make a claim for the employment insurance emergency response benefit in person or provide additional information about that claim.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.1302 (src:2894-2895)
GIVEN `the adaptation has not ceased to apply under section 153.14` IS A BOOLEAN
      `has provided the Minister with the required information in respect of the claim` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission requires the claimant to be at a suitable place at a suitable time to make the claim in person or provide additional information` IS A BOOLEAN
      `has complied with that requirement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 153.1302 as adapted s 50(1) the claimant is not eligible until they provide the information or comply` IF
        `the adaptation has not ceased to apply under section 153.14`
    AND (   NOT (`has provided the Minister with the required information in respect of the claim`)
         OR (`the Commission requires the claimant to be at a suitable place at a suitable time to make the claim in person or provide additional information` AND NOT (`has complied with that requirement`)))

-- src:2894 | 153.1302 For the purposes of applying paragraph 153.6(1)(a), section 50 is adapted as follows:
-- src:2895 | Eligibility — employment insurance emergency response benefit50(1)A claimant who does not provide the Minister with the required information in respect of a claim for the employment insurance emergency response benefit or fails to comply with the requirement under subsection (2) is not eligible for the employment insurance emergency response benefit until they provide the information or comply with the requirement.Making claim or providing information in person(2)The Commission may require a claimant or group or class of claimants to be at a suitable place at a suitable time in order to make a claim for the employment insurance emergency response benefit in person or provide additional information about that claim.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.1302 (src:2894-2895)
GIVEN `the adaptation has not ceased to apply under section 153.14` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claim or the information concerns the employment insurance emergency response benefit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 153.1302 as adapted s 50(2) the Commission may require the claimant to be at a suitable place at a suitable time` IF
        `the adaptation has not ceased to apply under section 153.14`
    AND `the claim or the information concerns the employment insurance emergency response benefit`

§ `Section 153.1303 - section 52 as adapted: decisions about money paid or not paid`

-- src:2897 | 153.1303 (1) For the purposes of applying paragraph 153.6(1)(a), subsection 52(2) is adapted as follows:
-- src:2898 | Decision(2)If the Commission decides that a person has received money by way of the employment insurance emergency response benefit for which the person was not eligible, or has not received money for which the person was eligible, the Commission must calculate the amount of the money and notify the claimant of its decision.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.1303(1) (src:2897-2898)
GIVEN `the adaptation has not ceased to apply under section 153.14` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission decides that the person has received money by way of the emergency response benefit for which the person was not eligible` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission decides that the person has not received money for which the person was eligible` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 153.1303 as adapted s 52(2) the Commission must calculate the amount and notify the claimant of its decision` IF
        `the adaptation has not ceased to apply under section 153.14`
    AND (   `the Commission decides that the person has received money by way of the emergency response benefit for which the person was not eligible`
         OR `the Commission decides that the person has not received money for which the person was eligible`)

-- src:2900 | (2) For the purposes of applying paragraph 153.6(1)(a), subsection 52(4) is adapted as follows:
-- src:2901 | Amount payable(4)If the Commission decides that a person was eligible to receive money by way of the employment insurance emergency response benefit, and the money was not paid, the amount calculated is payable to the claimant.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.1303(2) (src:2900-2901)
GIVEN `the adaptation has not ceased to apply under section 153.14` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission decides that the person was eligible to receive money by way of the emergency response benefit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the money was not paid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount calculated` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `s 153.1303 as adapted s 52(4) the amount payable to the claimant` IS
    IF     `the adaptation has not ceased to apply under section 153.14`
       AND `the Commission decides that the person was eligible to receive money by way of the emergency response benefit`
       AND `the money was not paid`
    THEN JUST `the amount calculated`
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 153.1305 - section 112 as adapted: reconsideration`

-- (1): a claimant or other person who is the subject of a decision, or the employer of the claimant, may request
-- reconsideration within 30 days after the day the decision is communicated to them, or within any further time the
-- Commission allows. The 30th day counts (fork F-ei6-10 of the keel's F4 reading); a request on the day the decision is
-- communicated is in time.
-- src:2904 | 153.1305 (1) For the purposes of applying paragraph 153.6(1)(d), subsection 112(1) is adapted as follows:
-- src:2905 | Reconsideration — Commission112(1)A claimant or other person who is the subject of a decision of the Commission, or the employer of the claimant, may make a request to the Commission in accordance with subsection (4) for a reconsideration of that decision at any time within(a)30 days after the day on which a decision is communicated to them; or(b)any further time that the Commission may allow.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.1305(1) (src:2904-2905)
GIVEN `the adaptation has not ceased to apply under section 153.14` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is the claimant or other person who is the subject of the decision, or the employer of the claimant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the decision is communicated to them` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the request is made` IS A DATE
      `the Commission has allowed any further time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 153.1305(1) as adapted s 112(1) the person may make a request for reconsideration` IF
        `the adaptation has not ceased to apply under section 153.14`
    AND `is the claimant or other person who is the subject of the decision, or the employer of the claimant`
    AND (   (    `the day on which the request is made` AT LEAST `the day on which the decision is communicated to them`
             AND `the day on which the request is made` AT MOST `the last day of` 30 `days after` `the day on which the decision is communicated to them`)
         OR `the Commission has allowed any further time`)

-- (2) adds s 112(4): the request must be in writing and contain the name and the social insurance number or business
-- number, the address and telephone number, the facsimile number and email address if any, the date the decision was
-- communicated, the reasons, and any relevant information not previously provided.
-- src:2907 | (2) For the purposes of applying paragraph 153.6(1)(d), section 112 is adapted by adding the following after subsection (3):
-- src:2908 | Reconsideration of a decision(4)A request for reconsideration of the decision must be in writing and contain the following information:(a)the name of the person making the request and their(i)social insurance number or the business number assigned to them by the Minister of National Revenue, as the case may be,(ii)address and telephone number, and(iii)facsimile number and email address, if any;(b)the date on which the decision was communicated to the person;(c)the reasons why the person is requesting a reconsideration of the decision; and(d)any relevant information that was not previously provided to the Commission.Filing of request for reconsideration(5)A request for reconsideration must be filed with the Commission at the address, facsimile number or email address — or in accordance with the electronic filing procedure — provided by the Commission on the website of the Department of Employment and Social Development.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.1305(2) (src:2907-2908)
GIVEN `the adaptation has not ceased to apply under section 153.14` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request contains the name of the person making it and their social insurance number or the business number assigned to them by the Minister of National Revenue` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request contains their address and telephone number` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request contains their facsimile number and email address, if they have any` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request contains the date on which the decision was communicated to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request contains the reasons why the person is requesting a reconsideration of the decision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request contains any relevant information that was not previously provided to the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 153.1305(2) as added s 112(4) the request for reconsideration is in the form required` IF
        `the adaptation has not ceased to apply under section 153.14`
    AND `the request is in writing`
    AND `the request contains the name of the person making it and their social insurance number or the business number assigned to them by the Minister of National Revenue`
    AND `the request contains their address and telephone number`
    AND `the request contains their facsimile number and email address, if they have any`
    AND `the request contains the date on which the decision was communicated to the person`
    AND `the request contains the reasons why the person is requesting a reconsideration of the decision`
    AND `the request contains any relevant information that was not previously provided to the Commission`

-- (2) adds s 112(5): the request must be filed with the Commission at the address, facsimile number or email address,
-- or in accordance with the electronic filing procedure, that the Commission provides on the website of the
-- Department of Employment and Social Development.
-- src:2908 | Reconsideration of a decision(4)A request for reconsideration of the decision must be in writing and contain the following information:(a)the name of the person making the request and their(i)social insurance number or the business number assigned to them by the Minister of National Revenue, as the case may be,(ii)address and telephone number, and(iii)facsimile number and email address, if any;(b)the date on which the decision was communicated to the person;(c)the reasons why the person is requesting a reconsideration of the decision; and(d)any relevant information that was not previously provided to the Commission.Filing of request for reconsideration(5)A request for reconsideration must be filed with the Commission at the address, facsimile number or email address — or in accordance with the electronic filing procedure — provided by the Commission on the website of the Department of Employment and Social Development.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.1305(2) (src:2908)
GIVEN `the adaptation has not ceased to apply under section 153.14` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request is filed with the Commission at the address, facsimile number or email address provided by the Commission on the website of the Department of Employment and Social Development` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request is filed in accordance with the electronic filing procedure provided by the Commission on that website` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 153.1305(2) as added s 112(5) the request for reconsideration is filed as required` IF
        `the adaptation has not ceased to apply under section 153.14`
    AND (   `the request is filed with the Commission at the address, facsimile number or email address provided by the Commission on the website of the Department of Employment and Social Development`
         OR `the request is filed in accordance with the electronic filing procedure provided by the Commission on that website`)

§ `Section 153.1306 - write-off of amounts wrongly paid`

-- (1): an amount payable under section 43 may be written off by the Commission if any of (a) to (f).
-- (1)(e): the overpayment does not arise from the debtor's error or false or misleading declaration (whether or not the
-- debtor knew it) but from (i) a retrospective decision or ruling under Part IV or (ii) the Commission providing a
-- weekly amount above $500.
-- src:2915 | (e) the overpayment does not arise from an error made by the debtor or as a result of a false or misleading declaration or representation made by the debtor, whether the debtor knew it to be false or misleading or not, but arises from
-- src:2916 | (i) a retrospective decision or ruling made under Part IV, or
-- src:2917 | (ii) provision by the Commission of a weekly employment insurance emergency response benefit amount in excess of the amount referred to in subsection 153.10(1); or
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.1306(1)(e) (src:2915-2917)
GIVEN `the overpayment arises from an error made by the debtor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the overpayment arises from a false or misleading declaration or representation made by the debtor, whether the debtor knew it to be false or misleading or not` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the overpayment arises from a retrospective decision or ruling made under Part IV` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the overpayment arises from provision by the Commission of a weekly emergency response benefit amount in excess of the amount referred to in subsection 153.10(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 153.1306(1)(e) the overpayment does not arise from the debtor's error or declaration but from a retrospective ruling or an excess weekly amount` IF
        NOT (`the overpayment arises from an error made by the debtor`)
    AND NOT (`the overpayment arises from a false or misleading declaration or representation made by the debtor, whether the debtor knew it to be false or misleading or not`)
    AND (   `the overpayment arises from a retrospective decision or ruling made under Part IV`
         OR `the overpayment arises from provision by the Commission of a weekly emergency response benefit amount in excess of the amount referred to in subsection 153.10(1)`)

-- (1)(f): "the Commission considers" that, having regard to all the circumstances, (i) the amount is uncollectable,
-- (ii) repayment would cause undue hardship, or (iii) the administrative costs would likely equal or exceed it.
-- That is the Commission's judgment: a BOOLEAN input, never guessed.
-- src:2918 | (f) the Commission considers that, having regard to all the circumstances,
-- src:2919 | (i) the amount is uncollectable,
-- src:2920 | (ii) the repayment of the amount would result in undue hardship to the debtor, or
-- src:2921 | (iii) the administrative costs of collecting the amount would likely equal or exceed the amount to be collected.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.1306(1)(f) (src:2918-2921)
GIVEN `the Commission considers, having regard to all the circumstances, that the amount is uncollectable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission considers, having regard to all the circumstances, that the repayment of the amount would result in undue hardship to the debtor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission considers, having regard to all the circumstances, that the administrative costs of collecting the amount would likely equal or exceed the amount to be collected` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 153.1306(1)(f) the Commission considers that the amount is uncollectable or that collecting it would be unduly hard or costly` IF
       `the Commission considers, having regard to all the circumstances, that the amount is uncollectable`
    OR `the Commission considers, having regard to all the circumstances, that the repayment of the amount would result in undue hardship to the debtor`
    OR `the Commission considers, having regard to all the circumstances, that the administrative costs of collecting the amount would likely equal or exceed the amount to be collected`

-- src:2910 | 153.1306 (1) An amount payable under section 43 may be written off by the Commission if
-- src:2911 | (a) the amount does not exceed $100;
-- src:2912 | (b) the debtor is deceased;
-- src:2913 | (c) the debtor is a discharged bankrupt;
-- src:2914 | (d) the debtor is an undischarged bankrupt in respect of whom the final dividend has been paid and the trustee has been discharged;
-- src:2915 | (e) the overpayment does not arise from an error made by the debtor or as a result of a false or misleading declaration or representation made by the debtor, whether the debtor knew it to be false or misleading or not, but arises from
-- src:2916 | (i) a retrospective decision or ruling made under Part IV, or
-- src:2917 | (ii) provision by the Commission of a weekly employment insurance emergency response benefit amount in excess of the amount referred to in subsection 153.10(1); or
-- src:2918 | (f) the Commission considers that, having regard to all the circumstances,
-- src:2919 | (i) the amount is uncollectable,
-- src:2920 | (ii) the repayment of the amount would result in undue hardship to the debtor, or
-- src:2921 | (iii) the administrative costs of collecting the amount would likely equal or exceed the amount to be collected.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.1306(1) (src:2910-2921)
GIVEN `the adaptation has not ceased to apply under section 153.14` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount payable under section 43` IS A NUMBER
      `the debtor is deceased` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the debtor is a discharged bankrupt` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the debtor is an undischarged bankrupt in respect of whom the final dividend has been paid and the trustee has been discharged` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (e) is met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (f) is met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 153.1306(1) the Commission may write off the amount payable under section 43` IF
        `the adaptation has not ceased to apply under section 153.14`
    AND (   `the amount payable under section 43` AT MOST 100
         OR `the debtor is deceased`
         OR `the debtor is a discharged bankrupt`
         OR `the debtor is an undischarged bankrupt in respect of whom the final dividend has been paid and the trustee has been discharged`
         OR `paragraph (e) is met`
         OR `paragraph (f) is met`)

-- (2): the portion of an amount owing under section 47 received before the Commission notifies the debtor of the
-- overpayment may be written off if the overpayment does not arise from the debtor's error or false or misleading
-- declaration, and arises from (i) a delay or error of the Commission, (ii) retrospective control procedures or a
-- retrospective review, (iii) an error in the employer's record of employment, (iv) the employer's incorrect
-- calculation of insurable earnings, or (v) an error in insuring the debtor's employment or other activity.
-- src:2922 | (2) The portion of an amount owing under section 47 in respect of the employment insurance emergency response benefit received before the Commission notifies the debtor of the overpayment may be written off by the Commission if
-- src:2923 | (a) the overpayment does not arise from an error made by the debtor or as a result of a false or misleading declaration or representation made by the debtor, whether the debtor knew it to be false or misleading or not; and
-- src:2924 | (b) the overpayment arises as a result of
-- src:2925 | (i) a delay or error made by the Commission in processing a claim for the employment insurance emergency response benefit,
-- src:2926 | (ii) retrospective control procedures or a retrospective review initiated by the Commission,
-- src:2927 | (iii) an error made on the record of employment by the employer,
-- src:2928 | (iv) an incorrect calculation by the employer of the debtor’s insurable earnings, or
-- src:2929 | (v) an error in insuring the employment or other activity of the debtor.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.1306(2) (src:2922-2929)
GIVEN `the adaptation has not ceased to apply under section 153.14` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the overpayment arises from an error made by the debtor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the overpayment arises from a false or misleading declaration or representation made by the debtor, whether the debtor knew it to be false or misleading or not` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the overpayment arises from a delay or error made by the Commission in processing a claim for the emergency response benefit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the overpayment arises from retrospective control procedures or a retrospective review initiated by the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the overpayment arises from an error made on the record of employment by the employer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the overpayment arises from an incorrect calculation by the employer of the debtor's insurable earnings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the overpayment arises from an error in insuring the employment or other activity of the debtor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 153.1306(2) the Commission may write off the portion of the amount owing under section 47 received before notification` IF
        `the adaptation has not ceased to apply under section 153.14`
    AND NOT (`the overpayment arises from an error made by the debtor`)
    AND NOT (`the overpayment arises from a false or misleading declaration or representation made by the debtor, whether the debtor knew it to be false or misleading or not`)
    AND (   `the overpayment arises from a delay or error made by the Commission in processing a claim for the emergency response benefit`
         OR `the overpayment arises from retrospective control procedures or a retrospective review initiated by the Commission`
         OR `the overpayment arises from an error made on the record of employment by the employer`
         OR `the overpayment arises from an incorrect calculation by the employer of the debtor's insurable earnings`
         OR `the overpayment arises from an error in insuring the employment or other activity of the debtor`)

§ `Sections 153.1307 to 153.13091 - sections 112.1, 126 and 138 and regulation 27 as adapted`

-- A decision under s 153.1306 is not subject to review under s 112: the person has no power to ask for a reconsideration.
-- src:2931 | 153.1307 For the purposes of applying paragraph 153.6(1)(d), section 112.1 is adapted as follows:
-- src:2932 | Decision not reviewable112.1A decision of the Commission under section 153.1306 is not subject to review under section 112.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.1307 (src:2931-2932)
GIVEN `the adaptation has not ceased to apply under section 153.14` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision is a decision of the Commission under section 153.1306` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 153.1307 as adapted s 112.1 the decision is not subject to review under section 112` IF
        `the adaptation has not ceased to apply under section 153.14`
    AND `the decision is a decision of the Commission under section 153.1306`

-- 126(1) before paragraph (a): an unpaid amount payable under Part I, II, VII.1 or VIII.4 may be certified by the
-- Commission. The rest of s 126(1) is outside this piece (ei4).
-- src:2934 | 153.1308 (1) For the purposes of applying paragraph 153.6(1)(d), the portion of subsection 126(1) before paragraph (a) is adapted as follows:
-- src:2935 | Certificates126(1)An amount or part of an amount payable under Part I, II, VII.1 or VIII.4 that has not been paid may be certified by the Commission
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.1308(1) (src:2934-2935)
GIVEN `the adaptation has not ceased to apply under section 153.14` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Part under which the amount is payable` IS A `Part of the Act`
      `the amount has not been paid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 153.1308 as adapted s 126(1) the Commission may certify the unpaid amount` IF
        `the adaptation has not ceased to apply under section 153.14`
    AND `the amount has not been paid`
    AND (   `the Part under which the amount is payable` EQUALS `Part I`
         OR `the Part under which the amount is payable` EQUALS `Part II`
         OR `the Part under which the amount is payable` EQUALS `Part VII.1`
         OR `the Part under which the amount is payable` EQUALS `Part VIII.4`)

-- src:2937 | (2) For the purposes of applying paragraph 153.6(1)(d), subsection 126(2) is adapted as follows:
-- src:2938 | Judgments(2)On production to the Federal Court, the resulting certificate shall be registered in the Court and when registered has the same force and effect, and all proceedings may be taken, as if the certificate were a judgment obtained in the Court for a debt of the amount specified in the certificate.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.1308(2) (src:2937-2938)
GIVEN `the adaptation has not ceased to apply under section 153.14` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate has been produced to the Federal Court and registered in the Court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 153.1308 as adapted s 126(2) the certificate has the force and effect of a judgment of the Federal Court for a debt of the amount specified` IF
        `the adaptation has not ceased to apply under section 153.14`
    AND `the certificate has been produced to the Federal Court and registered in the Court`

-- 138: every person employed in insurable employment and every self-employed person must have a Social Insurance
-- Number assigned under an Act of Parliament.
-- src:2940 | 153.1309 For the purposes of applying paragraph 153.6(1)(d), section 138 is adapted as follows:
-- src:2941 | Obligation138Every person employed in insurable employment and every self-employed person must have a Social Insurance Number that has been assigned to that person under an Act of Parliament.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.1309 (src:2940-2941)
GIVEN `the adaptation has not ceased to apply under section 153.14` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is employed in insurable employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is a self-employed person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 153.1309 as adapted s 138 the person must have a Social Insurance Number assigned under an Act of Parliament` IF
        `the adaptation has not ceased to apply under section 153.14`
    AND (`is employed in insurable employment` OR `is a self-employed person`)

-- reg 27(1) and (2): "Part I, VII.1 or VIII" is read as "Part VIII.4" (a reading rule: the Part to put in its place).
-- src:2943 | 153.13091 For the purposes of applying paragraph 153.6(1)(e), subsections 27(1) and (2) of the Employment Insurance Regulations are adapted so that the reference to “Part I, VII.1 or VIII” means “Part VIII.4”.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.13091 (src:2943)
GIVETH A `Part of the Act`
`s 153.13091 the Part that subsections 27(1) and (2) of the Regulations name for the emergency response benefit` MEANS `Part VIII.4`

§ `Section 153.1310 - special rules for people already on benefits`

-- The rules apply to a person who made an initial claim for benefits referred to in paragraph 153.5(3)(a) and who
-- either had, before this Part came into force retroactively, a benefit period established on or after March 15, 2020
-- with respect to those benefits, or would have had one but for this Part coming into force on March 15, 2020.
-- src:2947 | 153.1310 The following rules apply to a person who made an initial claim for benefits in respect of any of the benefits referred to in paragraph 153.5(3)(a) and who either had, before the coming into force retroactively of this Part, a benefit period established on or after March 15, 2020 with respect to the benefits for which the claim was made, or who would have had, but for the coming into force of this Part on March 15, 2020, a benefit period established on or after that same date with respect to the benefits for which the claim was made:
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.1310 (src:2947)
GIVEN `made an initial claim for benefits in respect of benefits referred to in paragraph 153.5(3)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `had, before the coming into force retroactively of this Part, a benefit period established on or after March 15, 2020 with respect to the benefits for which the claim was made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `would have had, but for the coming into force of this Part on March 15, 2020, a benefit period established on or after that date with respect to the benefits for which the claim was made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 153.1310 the special rules apply to the person` IF
        `made an initial claim for benefits in respect of benefits referred to in paragraph 153.5(3)(a)`
    AND (   `had, before the coming into force retroactively of this Part, a benefit period established on or after March 15, 2020 with respect to the benefits for which the claim was made`
         OR `would have had, but for the coming into force of this Part on March 15, 2020, a benefit period established on or after that date with respect to the benefits for which the claim was made`)

-- (a): the person is deemed to have made a claim for the benefit under s 153.8.
-- src:2948 | (a) the person is deemed to have made a claim for the employment insurance emergency response benefit under section 153.8;
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.1310(a) (src:2948)
GIVEN `the special rules of section 153.1310 apply to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 153.1310(a) the person is deemed to have made a claim for the emergency response benefit under section 153.8` IF
    `the special rules of section 153.1310 apply to the person`

-- (b): the rules of Part VIII.4 apply to the claim, except the rule that a claim be made in accordance with 153.8(1).
-- src:2949 | (b) the rules set out in Part VIII.4 apply to a claim for the employment insurance emergency response benefit, with the exception of the rule requiring that a claim be made in accordance with subsection 153.8(1); and
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.1310(b) (src:2949)
GIVEN `the special rules of section 153.1310 apply to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 153.1310(b) the person must make the claim in accordance with subsection 153.8(1)` IF
    NOT (`the special rules of section 153.1310 apply to the person`)

-- (c)(i): for each week of benefits referred to in paragraph 153.5(3)(a), the person is paid the difference between
-- $500 (subsection 153.10(1)) and the benefits received for the week. (c)(ii): an amount received above $500 is
-- deemed to be $500, and section 44 does not apply to the excess.
-- src:2950 | (c) the benefits referred to in paragraph 153.5(3)(a) received on or after March 15, 2020 are deemed to be the employment insurance emergency response benefit and, as the case may be,
-- src:2951 | (i) the person is to be paid, for each week for which they receive the benefits referred to in paragraph 153.5(3)(a), an amount of employment insurance emergency response benefit that is equal to the difference between the amount set out in subsection 153.10(1) and the amount of benefits that they received for the week in question, and
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.1310(c)(i) (src:2950-2951)
GIVEN `the special rules of section 153.1310 apply to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount of benefits referred to in paragraph 153.5(3)(a) received for the week` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `s 153.1310(c)(i) the amount of the emergency response benefit to be paid for the week` IS
    IF `the special rules of section 153.1310 apply to the person`
    THEN JUST (500 MINUS (IF `the amount of benefits referred to in paragraph 153.5(3)(a) received for the week` GREATER THAN 500 THEN 500 ELSE `the amount of benefits referred to in paragraph 153.5(3)(a) received for the week`))
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2952 | (ii) each amount of benefits received for a week that exceeds the amount set out in subsection 153.10(1) is deemed to be equal to the amount set out in that subsection and section 44 does not apply to any amount of benefits received for a week that exceeds the amount set out in subsection 153.10(1).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.1310(c)(ii) (src:2952)
GIVEN `the special rules of section 153.1310 apply to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount of benefits referred to in paragraph 153.5(3)(a) received for the week` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `s 153.1310(c)(ii) the amount of benefits received for the week, as deemed` IS
    IF `the special rules of section 153.1310 apply to the person`
    THEN JUST (IF `the amount of benefits referred to in paragraph 153.5(3)(a) received for the week` GREATER THAN 500 THEN 500 ELSE `the amount of benefits referred to in paragraph 153.5(3)(a) received for the week`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2952 | (ii) each amount of benefits received for a week that exceeds the amount set out in subsection 153.10(1) is deemed to be equal to the amount set out in that subsection and section 44 does not apply to any amount of benefits received for a week that exceeds the amount set out in subsection 153.10(1).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.1310(c)(ii) (src:2952)
GIVEN `the special rules of section 153.1310 apply to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount of benefits referred to in paragraph 153.5(3)(a) received for the week` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `s 153.1310(c)(ii) the amount of benefits received for the week to which section 44 does not apply` IS
    IF     `the special rules of section 153.1310 apply to the person`
       AND `the amount of benefits referred to in paragraph 153.5(3)(a) received for the week` GREATER THAN 500
    THEN JUST (`the amount of benefits referred to in paragraph 153.5(3)(a) received for the week` MINUS 500)
    ELSE NOTHING
